{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055503-fae-touched-and-court-contracts","id":1055503,"title":"Fae Touched and Court Contracts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-26T19:09:48-08:00","id":1055503,"title":"Fae Touched and Court Contracts","content":"It occurs to me that Fae Touched are better off going after Court Contracts then Goblin or most Universal Contracts. <br /> <br /> Some universal contracts have their effect entirely based on your wyrd. So not only does having a wyrd of zero penalized the activation roll, but if the effect is measured by x Wyrd even a success roll with have absolutely no effect. <br /> <br /> So some contracts are straight up traps for Fae Touched to take. <br /> <br /> But Fae Touched can join courts and as such qualify for Mantle Merit, so getting 5 dots in your Mantle and taking Court contracts as well as a few select Universal Contracts like Phantom Glory that Wyrd doesn't effect much beyond the activation roll, are your best choices. <br /> <br /> Activating a Court Contract is Skill + Attribute + Mantle and I doubt that any effects of the contract are expressed as x Wyrd so no trap options that don't work. <br /> <br /> So a Fae Touched with contract of emotion (Faith) with mantle 5 is likely equal to a changeling with mantle 5.<br /> <br /> So say they have equal attributes and skills too, say \u2022\u2022 in the relevant ones. <br /> <br /> They both have 2 + 2 + 5 activation roll. That pretty good for a Fae Touched.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T20:03:46-08:00","id":1055514,"title":"","content":"So the Fae-Touched have more incentive to join a court than go courtless. Makes sense.<br /> <br /> Do we have anything on Goblin Contracts, though? The Fae-Touched might not even be able to learn them in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T21:12:43-08:00","id":1055527,"title":"","content":"Be pretty hard for them to earn Mantle 5 though","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar792